THM-410 tournament witness interpretation
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
In a transitive p-vertex tournament, reverse only the long edge 0 -> p-1.
THM-410 says every interior vertex v with 0 < v < p-1 creates one
cyclic triangle 0 -> v -> p-1 -> 0, so #C3 = p-2.
For the reversed long edge p-1 -> 0, the pair-witness split is
sigma=0, lambda=p-2, delta=0: all p-2 witnesses are cyclic.
This is a structural horizon, not a Hamiltonian-path count.

Typed bridge
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Q_p(0)=p is a boundary prime.
Q_p(1)..Q_p(p-2) are the p-2 interior primality witnesses.
Q_p(p-1)=p^2 is the forced boundary composite.
d=4p-1 is the class-number-one / unique-factorization side channel.
The tournament analogue is an interval with p-2 interior witnesses.

Tournament Analysis
------------------------------------------------------------------------------
vertices = class_number_one_factorization, euler_prime_horizon, heegner_discriminant_map, interval_reversal_long_edge, pair_witness_n_minus_2, first_composite_boundary, raw_number_list
pairwise observable = which lens preserves more typed information
switch/gauge = orient A -> B when A explains B without scalar collapse
tie Hamiltonian path = class_number_one_factorization > euler_prime_horizon > heegner_discriminant_map > interval_reversal_long_edge > pair_witness_n_minus_2 > first_composite_boundary > raw_number_list
